      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14132963/assets/e31063e3f0bf77bf87c023f19051ae2c35837bbe3c1e37443b6f4367fd84e68d.png)\n\nIf each cube represents $1$ cubic unit, what is the volume of the figure?",
      "worked_solution": "The figure consists of $3$ rows, and each row has $6$ cubes.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14132963/assets/900ff63f2c2e730bbc2a914fb099646e10f7c36c8eb9008c051343d8dd1a45af.png)\n\nSo, there are $6\\times 3=18$ cubes in total.\n\nTherefore, the volume of the figure is $18$ cubic units.",
